WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Seven workspaces
Manage apps and files, open screen sessions and diagnose your phone.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.400
Have only an APK?
Open and inspect a local APK without connecting a device.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.920
Paste a list into Apps
The search field narrows the table to matching packages.

4
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.400
Work in the right profile
Inspect permissions and components, or select several apps for a batch action.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.200
Read the debloat evidence
The list explains its classification, dependencies and available alternatives.

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.000
Freeze or disable
Freeze suspends the app. Background services may continue. You can unfreeze or re-enable it later.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.800
Save the whole APK set
A split app needs its base APK and installed splits. Include app folders separately.

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.600
Back up a group
Save a package-selection preset and review the result for each app. Protected data and cache require root.

9
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.320
From a backup
Check the recorded contents, version and location, then restore supported parts to the selected profile.

10
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.000
From the phone
Restore a removed system package if its APK still exists. This brings back the app only.

11
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.600
Compare before installing
Inspect changes to versions, permissions, signing details and files.

12
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.200
Example
The newer Notes APK requests notification permission. The inspector reads the package without launching it.

13
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.000
Find matches and evidence
Check tracker and library signatures, native architectures and the APK size breakdown.

14
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.800
Trace a domain to its source
Search extracted URLs and see which file contains each string. Actual device connections appear in Monitor.

15
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.520
Mirror or launch
Control the phone screen, or open a selected Android app in its own virtual display. Pin a window on top.

16
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.200
Camera and recording
Choose supported lenses, resolutions, frame rates and audio. Record supported sessions as MP4 or MKV.

17
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.920
For a touch-only game
Place the target over Jump in the touch editor, bind Space and save the game preset.

18
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.600
For native input
Use keyboard and mouse, PC-layout typing or a supported gamepad. Edit bindings and hotkeys as needed.

19
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.000
Choose either panel’s source
Open local folders, phone storage or Windows-accessible SMB shares. Keep frequent locations in tabs and bookmarks.

20
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.400
Find the file first
Search names or categories and preview supported images, video and audio.

21
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.720
Copy or move
Choose the source and destination, then follow progress in the task queue.

22
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.000
Resolve interruptions
Review conflicts, pause or resume work, and retry a failed transfer.

23
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.720
Set up Components
Locate or download ADB, Fastboot and optional scrcpy. Maintain the detection databases here.

24
00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.400
Select the device
Authorize USB or pair over Wi-Fi. Check device details, existing root access and supported Fastboot restart modes.

25
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.920
Export the records you choose
Preview contacts, SMS and call history. Save call records as CSV or JSON where Android permits access.

26
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.400
Share a piece of text
Transfer clipboard text between the PC and phone, or create a local text QR code.

27
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.200
Read device statistics
View reported CPU, memory, battery and interface traffic. Pause sampling or choose an interval.

28
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.000
Inspect a connection
See an app owner when Android exposes it. Optional local GeoIP data adds country and network information.

29
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.720
Gather diagnostics
Filter a Logcat snapshot, save logs or collect an Android bug report. Activity keeps operation results.

30
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.400
Use the console
Run an ADB or Android shell command on the selected device and read its output.

31
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.800
Write it once
Attach a personal label or note to a package. Its record appears when you see that package on another phone.

32
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.200
Keep the original context
See the source phone, profile, app version and record date. Notes stay on your computer.

33
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.600
Choose your layout
Adjust theme, density, corners, badge colors, toolbar and workspace order. Configure search and scanner links.

34
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.000
Start at your own pace
Install or extract a portable copy. Take the optional English tour, skip it or replay it later.

35
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.400
Get the Windows build
Find Setup, Portable and the illustrated guide in the project repository.

36
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.800
Tell us what worked
Device coverage is limited. For a bug report, include the steps, phone model, Android version and Windows version.
